  "cli_result_text": "Submitted the files needed to trace this issue:\n\n1. **`pkg/registry/core/rest/storage_core.go`** \u2014 origin of the exact error string; the `PostStartHook` func that races the repair controllers against a 1-minute timeout.\n2. **`staging/src/k8s.io/apiserver/pkg/server/hooks.go`** \u2014 `AddPostStartHookOrDie`/`postStartHookEntry`, which wires each PostStartHook to a `postStartHookHealthz` readyz check (the `poststarthook/start-service-ip-repair-controllers` name in the ticket's log comes from here).\n3. **`pkg/registry/core/service/ipallocator/controller/repairip.go`** \u2014 `RepairIPAddress.RunUntil`/`runOnce`, the actual controller that must complete a full sync (including waiting on the `defaultservicecidr` ServiceCIDR to exist) before calling `onFirstSuccess`, which is what unblocks the hook.\n4. **`staging/src/k8s.io/apiserver/pkg/server/healthz/healthz.go`** \u2014 readyz/healthz handler plumbing, including `informer-sync`, explaining the two check names seen together in the readyz failure.\n5. **`healthz_test.go`** \u2014 shows `postStartHookHealthz` and `delayedHealthCheck` semantics precisely.\n6. **`config.go`** \u2014 `Config.AddPostStartHookOrDie` wrapper.\n7. **`pkg/controlplane/apiserver/apis.go`** \u2014 where `legacyProvider.PostStartHook()` actually gets registered against `GenericAPIServer`.\n8. **`pkg/controlplane/instance.go`** \u2014 registers `start-kubernetes-service-cidr-controller`, the controller that must create the default ServiceCIDR object the repair controller polls for \u2014 the likely upgrade-window race (new v1.33 IPAddress/ServiceCIDR-aware repair controller waiting on a resource an old v1.32 peer hasn't created/synced yet).\n9. **`repairip_test.go`** \u2014 shows expected startup/sync sequencing for `RepairIPAddress`.\n10. **`pkg/registry/core/service/ipallocator/metaallocator.go`** \u2014 the allocator that returns \"forbidden: not yet ready to handle request\" for IPAddress objects while the meta-allocator hasn't finished initializing, matching the second log line in the ticket.",
